CLR (rocclr) H2D copy routing (gfx803): mirror of d2h-staged-copy.patch
for Host-to-Device transfers. Never pin pageable host memory for direct
SDMA transfer on gfx803 -- force the GPU-staging path for H2D copies.

WHY
---
Under PyTorch Host-to-Device copies (e.g. model.cuda() / tensor.to('cuda')),
HIP pins pageable host memory (userptr BOs) for transfers above
GPU_PINNED_MIN_XFER_SIZE. On gfx803 (Polaris), when that host buffer is
freed or unmapped, the Linux KFD MMU notifier evicts all user queues,
causing queue hangs, stuck packets, and "Memory access fault ... Page not present"
(read from TC0).

Disabling host pinning (forcing the staging path via kEnablePin = false and
routing registered hostMemory transfers through staged writeBuffer instead of
copyBuffer) keeps the MMU notifier idle and completely eliminates queue evictions
and in-flight page faults on H2D transfers.

Applies on top of d2h-staged-copy.patch.

diff --git a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp
--- a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocblit.cpp
@@ -140,7 +140,11 @@ bool DmaBlitManager::writeBuffer(const void* srcHost, device::Memory& dstMemory,
   if (copySize > 0) {
     address dstAddr = gpuMem(dstMemory).getDeviceMemory() + origin[0];
     const_address srcAddr = reinterpret_cast<const_address>(srcHost);
     constexpr bool kHostToDev = true;
-    constexpr bool enablePin = true;
+    // GFX803: never pin the host source for an H2D copy -- pinning pageable
+    // host memory causes KFD MMU notifier queue evictions and in-flight
+    // page faults on gfx803. Force the GPU-staging path.
+    constexpr bool enablePin = false;
     if (!hsaCopyStagedOrPinned(srcAddr, dstAddr, copySize, kHostToDev, copyMetadata, enablePin)) {
       LogError("DmaBlitManager:: writeBuffer copy failure!");
       return false;
@@ -176,8 +180,9 @@ bool DmaBlitManager::writeBufferRect(const void* srcHost, device::Memory& dstMemory,
         // Copy data from host to device - line by line
         const_address src = reinterpret_cast<const_address>(srcHost) + srcOffset;
         constexpr bool kHostToDev = true;
+        constexpr bool enablePin = false;
         bool retval =
-            hsaCopyStagedOrPinned(src, dst + dstOffset, size[0], kHostToDev, copyMetadata);
+            hsaCopyStagedOrPinned(src, dst + dstOffset, size[0], kHostToDev, copyMetadata, enablePin);
         if (!retval) {
           return retval;
         }
diff --git a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
--- a/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
+++ b/projects/clr/rocclr/device/rocm/rocvirtual.cpp
@@ -3266,8 +3266,13 @@ void VirtualGPU::submitWriteMemory(amd::WriteMemoryCommand& cmd) {
         size.c[0] *= elemSize;
       }
       if (hostMemory != nullptr) {
-        // Accelerated transfer without pinning
-        amd::Coord3D srcOrigin(offset);
-        result = blitMgr().copyBuffer(*hostMemory, *devMem, srcOrigin, origin, size,
-                                      cmd.isEntireMemory(), cmd.copyMetadata());
+        // GFX803: do NOT read the (registered/locked) host buffer directly
+        // from the copy engine via copyBuffer. Route through the staged
+        // writeBuffer to prevent MMU notifier queue evictions and in-flight
+        // page faults on gfx803.
+        const char* hostSrc = static_cast<const char*>(cmd.source());
+        result = blitMgr().writeBuffer(hostSrc, *devMem, origin, size,
+                                       cmd.isEntireMemory(), cmd.copyMetadata());
       } else {
         result = blitMgr().writeBuffer(src, *devMem, origin, size, cmd.isEntireMemory(),
                                        cmd.copyMetadata());
@@ -3520,8 +3525,14 @@ bool VirtualGPU::copyMemory(cl_command_type type, amd::Memory& srcMem, amd::Memo
         void* dstHost = dstDevMem->getDeviceMemory();
         result = blitMgr().readBuffer(*srcDevMem, dstHost, realSrcOrigin,
                                       realSize, entire, copyMetadata);
+      } else if (srcDevMem->isHostMemDirectAccess()) {
+        // GFX803: same as submitWriteMemory -- an H2D copy from a
+        // registered/locked host buffer must go through the staged
+        // writeBuffer, not the copy engine reading the host buffer directly.
+        const void* srcHost = srcDevMem->getDeviceMemory();
+        result = blitMgr().writeBuffer(srcHost, *dstDevMem, realDstOrigin,
+                                       realSize, entire, copyMetadata);
       } else {
         result = blitMgr().copyBuffer(*srcDevMem, *dstDevMem, realSrcOrigin, realDstOrigin,
                                       realSize, entire, copyMetadata);
       }
